<title>UK: GECC sets $250 million four-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>GECC sets $250 million four-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced</p>
<p>by lead manager Nikko.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT    $250 MLN	COUPON     6.25 PCT  MATURITY    27.MAR.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.241   PAY DATE    27.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.625     REOFFER    99.841    SPREAD	+4 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.40	PRAECIP     =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND THREE-YEAR U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
